.KEY DIR/A,STEP/K
.BRA {
.KET }
; up-git install: git 2.56.0 (clone, fetch and ls-remote over https via AmiSSL; local commands) in UP-Term:bin and UP-Term:share/git-core
; Run by this archive's Install (an Installer script), which asks the questions:
;   Execute <archive>/Files/install.dos <archive>/Files [STEP <part>]
; From a Shell without Installer the same line installs everything. The Installer
; runs the parts one at a time with STEP (tests/test_dist_addons.py holds the two to
; the same list); the first part, check, stops the install when up-term.lha is
; missing or too old (the reason is in ENV:UPTCHECK).
FailAt 21
; the archive's Files drawer: every name below is relative to it
CD "{DIR}"
; every write into UP-Term: goes through UPTREAL: (UP-Term: may be a multi-directory assign: it writes to the first one)
; @include dist/common/@RECORDRESOLVE@
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Skip {STEP}
EndIf
; @include dist/common/@CHECKFRAG@
Lab copy-git
; git (bin/git and its helpers, share/git-core/templates): git keeps its objects as long-named files, so the
; UP-Term volume needs long file names: FFS in long-name mode (DOS7), PFS3 or SFS. OFS and plain FFS
; stop at 30 characters, too short for git's object files.
; userland holds what dist/slim.txt names; Copy of a drawer copies what is in it.
MakeDir >NIL: UPTREAL:bin
MakeDir >NIL: UPTREAL:lib
MakeDir >NIL: UPTREAL:licenses
Copy userland UPTREAL: ALL CLONE QUIET
If WARN
  Quit 20
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
; @include dist/common/record.dos
Echo "git installed: type  git  in an UP-Term window (vsh)."
